    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **59 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skipped.**\n\n## Summary\n\nThe registration-date business-day rule now rolls forward past public holidays in addition to weekends.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/common/BusinessDays.java`:\n\n- Added the fixed public-holiday set: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `rollToBusinessDay` as a loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or a listed holiday**. This correctly handles runs of consecutive non-business days (e.g. `2026-12-25` Friday \u2192 skip \u2192 weekend \u2192 `2026-12-28` holiday \u2192 `2026-12-29`).\n\nThis matches the test-side `HOLIDAYS`/`toBusinessDay` helper in `AcceptanceBase` and the intent documented in `Cp47Tests`. The prior implementation only skipped weekends and returned the raw weekday otherwise.\n\nNo new production classes or endpoints were needed \u2014 the rule lives in the existing shared helper called from `BuildOwner`, so the change flows through the whole owner-registration pipeline automatically. The existing black-box acceptance tests (`Cp07`, `Cp20`, `Cp47`) and the full suite pass.\n\nOne note: the holiday list is hard-coded for calendar year 2026 (as the spec dictates), so dates in other years are unaffected by the holiday rule \u2014 consistent with the test fixtures, which are all pinned to 2026.",
